# GUNUCO UI Implementation Document

This file is the primary implementation reference for screens, states, fields, and operational flows.

============================================================
1. CURRENT SYSTEM SCOPE
============================================================

Product: GUNUCO Multi-Category Ordering and Delivery System

Current operating model:
- One production house accepts and fulfils every order. `Pickup-at-Store` is the customer-facing label for collection there; it is not a separate store entity.
- Owner Admin is the highest role and has full control and final authority. Main Admin manages categories, subcategories, products, add-ons, orders, production, and delivery. Branch Admin is restricted to assigned locations.
- Delivery Partners collect only `Doorstep-Delivery` orders from the production house; `Pickup-at-Store` orders remain in the Admin pickup queue.
- `Cakes` is the active launch parent category. Its configurable launch subcategories are `GUNUCO PREMIUM`, `Cakes & Wedding Cakes`, and `Cookies`.
- GUNUCO PREMIUM contains GUNUCO's special, curated cake catalogue. Custom Cakes remain a dedicated cake request workflow.
- Main Admin can add, edit, activate, deactivate, and reorder parent categories and subcategories from the Admin Panel. Future parent categories may include Coffee, Pizza, and Burgers.
- Category names, hierarchy, product options, and navigation entries are configuration-driven and must not be hard-coded.
- Branch creation and transfers are feature-disabled at launch, but locations, assignments, orders, POS, fulfilment, quotas, and reporting are location-ready from the first release.

Current panels:
1. Main Admin Panel
2. Delivery Partner Panel
3. Customer Support Panel

Portal entry points:
- Owner Admin: `https://owner.gunuco.com/login`
- Main Admin and Branch Admin: `https://admin.gunuco.com/login`
- Customer Support Agent: `https://support.gunuco.com/login`

