Access rule:
- Owner Admin sees every menu item and controls branches, Global POS, admin-location assignments, and owner-only global rules.
- Main Admin sees operational sections and can manage categories, subcategories, products, pricing, add-ons, Branch Admins, and delivery partners. Owner-only actions are hidden or read-only.
- Branch Admin sees assigned-location Dashboard, Point of Sale, Orders, Production Queue, Delivery Partners, pickup, and delivery operations. Definition-level and global controls are hidden.
- Delivery Partner never enters this panel.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 ADMIN DASHBOARD
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Central control for production-house orders, preparation, delivery, payments, and exceptions.

Required cards:
- Today's Orders
- Today's Revenue
- Cakes parent orders with configurable subcategory breakdowns
- Custom Cakes Orders
- Awaiting Acceptance
- Preparing
- Ready for Delivery
- Deliveries Pending
- Delivering
- Delivered Today

Top controls:
- Accept Orders ON/OFF
- Active parent-category and subcategory availability controls generated from configuration
- Accept Custom Cakes ON/OFF
- Acceptance modes generated for each active parent category or subcategory
- Custom Cakes Acceptance Mode: Automatic / Manual
- Delivery Assignment Mode: Automatic / Manual

ORDER CONTROLS BOARD

The dashboard must contain a visible Order Controls board:

```text
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| ORDER CONTROLS                                                           |
| Accept Orders                         [ON/OFF]                            |
| Active Category/Subcategory           [Automatic | Manual]                |
| Custom Cakes Acceptance               [Automatic | Manual]                |
| Delivery Assignment                   [Automatic | Manual]                |
|                                                                          |
| DAILY LIMITS                                                             |
| All Orders                            [Current / Limit] [Edit Limit]      |
| Each Active Category/Subcategory      [Current / Limit] [Edit Limit]      |
| Custom Cakes                          [Current / Limit] [Edit Limit]      |
|                                                                          |
| Custom Cake Scheduling Window         [3 days minimum | 30 days maximum] |
| Eligible Cakes Subcategories          [ON/OFF] [Cutoff] [Slots]          |
| Fulfilment Methods       [Pickup-at-Store ON] [Doorstep-Delivery ON]     |
| Quota Reset                           [Midnight, configured timezone]     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

Control behavior:
- Automatic: accept a valid order immediately after availability, payment, requested quantity, delivery time, and every applicable daily limit pass validation.
- Manual: create the order as Not Accepted and place it in Awaiting Acceptance for Main Admin action.
- Main Admin can manually Accept or Reject an order waiting in Manual mode.
- Changing mode affects new orders only; it must not silently change existing orders.
- Global OFF overrides every acceptance mode and category.
- Daily limits are numeric values greater than zero and remain editable by Main Admin.
- Show live accepted quantity, configured limit, percentage used, and remaining capacity.
- Alert Main Admin at 80 percent usage and block acceptance when the requested quantity would exceed a limit.
- Reset daily usage at midnight in the configured production house timezone.
- Custom Cakes can be scheduled from 3 days (72 hours) through 30 days (720 hours) after order time.
- Reject a custom-cake request outside the inclusive 3-to-30-day scheduling window.

Delivery controls and visibility:
- Deliveries Pending counts orders with delivery status `Pending Assignment` or `Assigned`.
- Delivering counts orders with delivery status `Picked Up` or `Out for Delivery`.
- Delivered Today counts orders marked `Delivered` today.
- Dashboard and Orders tables show the assigned delivery partner name beside delivery status.
- Automatic assignment starts when an accepted order needs delivery; the rider is notified immediately and can view the future pickup time while production continues.
- Automatic assignment selects an Active and Online rider who accepts deliveries, has no conflicting pickup, serves the delivery area, and has the lowest active workload. Rating and distance break ties.
- The selected rider must accept within the configured timeout. Rejection or timeout automatically tries the next eligible rider.
- If no rider accepts, status remains `Pending Assignment` and Main Admin receives an alert.
- Manual mode leaves the order Pending Assignment until Main Admin selects a rider.
- Main Admin can override or reassign before pickup. Every attempt and reassignment is recorded.
- Automatic rider assignment runs only for `Doorstep-Delivery`; `Pickup-at-Store` never creates a rider assignment.

Customer fulfilment options:
- Before payment, the customer must choose exactly one option: `Pickup-at-Store` or `Doorstep-Delivery`.
- `Pickup-at-Store`: customer collects from the production house and delivery fee is always Rs 0.
- `Doorstep-Delivery`: customer enters an address and the server calculates road distance from the production house.
- Cakes and eligible Cakes subcategory doorstep fee: up to 5 km inclusive = Rs 0; over 5 km through 8 km = Rs 39; over 8 km through 10 km = Rs 59; over 10 km through 15 km = Rs 159.
- `Doorstep-Delivery` beyond 15 km is unavailable by default; show `Pickup-at-Store` or ask the customer to choose an address within range.
- Custom Cakes offer both `Pickup-at-Store` and `Doorstep-Delivery`, and both have Rs 0 delivery fee regardless of distance within the configured service area.
- Recalculate and display `Subtotal - Discount + Delivery Fee = Payable Total` immediately whenever the customer changes the option or doorstep address.
- Show the selected option, verified distance, delivery fee, address or store pickup instructions, selected time, and final payable total on the checkout review before enabling payment.
- Do not book a catalogue order until the customer reviews the recalculated total and completes either full payment or the required 50% advance. A Custom Cake request may be saved before payment for clarification, feasibility review, and quoting, but cannot enter production until accepted and the required booking payment is captured.
- Pickup lifecycle is `Pickup Scheduled -> Ready for Pickup -> Collected`.
- Customer-facing Order ID format is `YY-N`, with a minimum two-digit sequence: `26-01`, `26-02`, ... `26-888`. The sequence restarts at `01` each calendar year.
- Main Admin marks pickup orders Ready for Pickup. At collection, Admin enters the customer's Order ID and the server validates an exact match before enabling `Collected`.
- At the doorstep, the delivery partner enters the customer's Order ID and the server validates an exact match before enabling `Delivered`.
- No OTP or separate pickup code is used for either fulfilment option.
- Record who validated the Order ID, when it was validated, and whether validation occurred at the store or doorstep.
- Generate the yearly sequence atomically so simultaneous orders cannot receive duplicate IDs.
- Store collection/delivery completion and successful validation in one server transaction. Store validation is limited to an Owner Admin, Main Admin, or Branch Admin authorized for the order's location; doorstep validation is limited to the assigned rider.
- Validate the exact customer-facing Order ID only. OTP, pickup code, phone number, or a client-submitted success value cannot substitute for the server comparison.
- Rate-limit failed entries and alert Main Admin about repeated mismatches.
- Customer receives the Order ID, pickup address, map link, operating hours, and Ready for Pickup notification.

Cashless payment rules:
- Never offer Cash, Cash on Delivery, or cash payment at the store or doorstep.
- Before booking, customer chooses `Full Payment` or `50% Advance + 50% Balance`.
- Full Payment captures the complete payable total online.
- Split payment captures 50% online to book and displays the remaining 50% with a Pay Balance Online action.
- If currency rounding is required, round the advance to two decimals and calculate balance as `Payable Total - Advance Paid`.
- Production may proceed after a successful 50% advance, but handover and dispatch cannot proceed until Balance Due is Rs 0.
- Disable `Ready for Pickup` handover, `Picked Up`, `Out for Delivery`, Order ID completion validation, `Collected`, and `Delivered` while a balance remains.
- Same-day orders support both plans. Reserve the slot only after the full amount or 50% advance succeeds, and require balance payment online before the rider leaves or the customer collects.
- Main Admin sees Amount Paid, Balance Due, Balance Deadline, payment attempts, and payment-hold alerts.
- Delivery Partners see payment clearance status but never receive or record cash.

Same-day delivery controls:
- Same-day delivery applies only to eligible Cakes subcategories; Custom Cakes retain the 3-to-30-day rule.
- Main Admin controls same-day ON/OFF independently for each eligible Cakes subcategory.
- Main Admin sets the order cutoff time, minimum preparation lead time, same-day slot capacity, delivery slots, and service area.
- Each cake has an Allow Same-Day Delivery ON/OFF override.
- Same-day is offered only when global/category/product acceptance is ON, the cake supports it, the cutoff has not passed, preparation can finish before the selected slot, daily quotas have capacity, a delivery slot is available, and the address is serviceable.
- If same-day is unavailable, show the next available date or slot instead of accepting an impossible delivery time.

Quick actions:
- Add Cake
- Manage Categories
- Add Add-On
- Review Custom Cake
- Assign Delivery
- Create Offer

Recent orders columns:
- Order ID
- Parent Category
- Subcategory
- Customer
- Requested Delivery
- Amount
- Production Status
- Delivery Status
- Assigned Delivery Partner

Critical rule:
- If global Accept Orders is OFF, no new order from any category, subcategory, or Custom Cake workflow can be accepted.
- Passing validation in Automatic mode changes status directly to Accepted.
- Passing validation in Manual mode leaves status as Not Accepted until Main Admin accepts it.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.1A POINT OF SALE
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Provide assisted, cashless Pickup-at-Store ordering only when a customer at an authorized location cannot reasonably use the application.

Access and controls:
- Owner Admin, Main Admin, or Branch Admin may use POS only at an authorized location where Global POS and Location POS are both ON.
- Resolve location from the authenticated assignment; do not provide an unrestricted location selector.
- Require an exception reason: No mobile device, Device unavailable, Application unavailable, or Accessibility assistance.
- Mobile number may be omitted only for No mobile device, which requires a printed receipt.

Workspace:
- Cascading Parent Category and Subcategory filters generated from active location configuration
- Product search, image, availability, starting price, same-day eligibility, and remaining quota
- Product-schema controls; cake products show flavour, Egg/Eggless, sugar, flour, weight, and quantity
- Required and optional add-ons with quantity controls
- Cart edit, remove, clear, offer, option/add-on breakdown, subtotal, tax, and payable total
- Fixed Pickup-at-Store fulfilment and required pickup time
- Full Payment or 50% Advance + 50% Balance
- Card, UPI, Net Banking, Wallet, or Store Credit only
- Collect Online Payment; never show Cash, COD, Record Cash, or manual Mark Paid
- Payment pending, success, failure, retry, and payment-hold states
- Receipt preview, Print Receipt, Share Receipt, New Sale, and View Order

After successful booking payment and all server checks, create the ordinary order as Accepted in the shared location production queue. Record channel POS, location, operator, and exception reason. Failed or abandoned payments do not consume quota or generate a paid receipt.

