3.3 CAKE CATALOGUE
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Manage products under the Cakes parent and its configurable subcategories with their selectable options and add-ons.

Table columns:
- Image
- Cake Name
- Parent Category: Cakes
- Subcategory: GUNUCO PREMIUM, Cakes & Wedding Cakes, Cookies, or another configured Cakes subcategory
- Available Flavours
- Egg Options
- Sugar Type Options
- Flour Type Options
- Sizes
- Starting Price
- Orders Today
- Daily Quota
- Availability
- Edit

Add/Edit Cake fields:
- Cake Name
- Description
- Product Image
- Parent Category: Cakes
- Configurable Subcategory
- Flavours (multi-select)
- Egg Preferences: Egg and/or Eggless
- Sugar Types (multi-select)
- Flour Types: Maida and/or Wheat Flour
- Sizes/Weights (multi-select)
- Default Weight: 500g
- Default Egg Preference: Egg
- Default Sugar Type: Mishri
- Default Flour Type: Maida
- Default Quantity: 1
- Base Price
- Option Price Adjustments
- Discount Price
- Applicable Add-Ons and assignment preview
- Preparation Time
- Allow Same-Day Delivery ON/OFF
- Daily Quantity Quota
- Featured ON/OFF
- Available ON/OFF

Automatic price controls:
- Main Admin sets the base price for each cake.
- Main Admin manages an Ingredient Pricing Matrix for every cake.
- For Cakes and GUNUCO PREMIUM, the matrix stores a separate price for every option at 500g, 1kg, 2kg, and 3kg.
- The selected weight determines which flavour, Egg/Eggless, sugar type, and flour type prices are used.
- Main Admin can set a positive, zero, or negative ingredient price contribution for every selectable value.
- The customer sees the price and ingredient breakdown update immediately after every ingredient or quantity change; no Submit button is required to preview the new price.
- Formula for Cakes and GUNUCO PREMIUM: `Unit Price = Weight Base Price + Flavour Price for Weight + Egg Price for Weight + Sugar Price for Weight + Flour Price for Weight`.
- `Items Total = Unit Price x Quantity`.
- `Order Total = Items Total - Discount + Delivery Fee + Tax`, where configured.
- The server recalculates the final price from current admin rules before payment; client-submitted totals are never trusted.
- The order stores the selected ingredient names, IDs, individual price contributions, pricing rule version, calculation time, and final price so later admin changes do not alter an existing order.

Default menu configuration:
- When a customer opens a cake, preselect 500g, Mishri, Egg, Maida, and quantity 1.
- The cake's own flavour remains selected by default; if a cake supports multiple flavours, Main Admin chooses its default flavour.
- The catalogue `Starting Price` is the live server-calculated price for the default combination.
- Default Starting Price formula: `500g Base + Default Flavour 500g Price + Mishri 500g Price + Egg 500g Price + Maida 500g Price`.
- Mishri, Egg, and Maida are the minimum-price defaults. Main Admin may change their amounts, but publishing is blocked if another available option in the same group is cheaper than the configured default.
- Customer can change weight, flavour, Egg/Eggless, sugar type, flour type, and quantity. Every change recalculates the price immediately.
- A `Reset to Default` action restores the cake's configured default combination.

Customer price breakdown example:

```text
Chocolate Cake 500g Base                    Rs 500
Chocolate Flavour (500g)                    + Rs 40
Eggless (500g)                              + Rs 150
Mishri (500g)                               + Rs 40
Wheat Flour (500g)                          + Rs 150
---------------------------------------------------
Unit Price                                  Rs 880
Quantity: 2
Items Total                               Rs 1,760
```

Ingredient Pricing Matrix fields:
- Cake
- Ingredient Group: Flavour / Egg Preference / Sugar Type / Flour Type / Size
- Ingredient Option
- Weight: 500g / 1kg / 2kg / 3kg
- Price Contribution
- Available ON/OFF
- Effective From
- Updated By
- Updated At

Pricing behavior:
- Selecting, deselecting, or replacing any ingredient triggers a fresh quote.
- Changing quantity multiplies the newly calculated unit price.
- Unavailable ingredient combinations cannot be selected or quoted.
- Checkout requests a final server quote and rejects stale or tampered pricing.
- Existing paid or accepted orders retain their stored pricing snapshot.

