3.3B CATEGORIES & SUBCATEGORIES
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Allow Main Admin to manage the customer catalogue hierarchy without code or navigation changes. Owner Admin has full override and final authority; Branch Admin has no definition-level edit access.

Hierarchy table columns:
- Expand/collapse
- Category Code
- Display Name
- Parent Category
- Module/Type
- Status
- Display Order
- Active Locations
- Product Count
- Updated By and Updated At
- Actions

Actions:
- Add Parent Category
- Add Subcategory
- Edit
- Activate or Deactivate
- Reorder
- View Products
- Configure Locations

Create/edit fields:
- Unique code
- Display name
- Optional parent
- Description and image
- Category module/type
- Display order
- Acceptance mode
- Daily quota
- Same-day eligibility
- Active/Inactive status

Rules:
- Seed Cakes as the active parent with GUNUCO PREMIUM, Cakes & Wedding Cakes, and Cookies as active subcategories.
- Main Admin can later create Coffee, Pizza, Burgers, or any other parent/subcategory.
- Prevent selecting the current category or a descendant as its parent.
- Block destructive deletion when products or child categories depend on the record; use deactivation to preserve history.
- Deactivating a parent blocks new activity for descendants but preserves products and historical orders.
- Global activation does not automatically enable a category at every location.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.3C ADD-ONS
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Allow Main Admin to configure additional selectable or required items and pricing from the Admin Panel. Owner Admin has full authority; Branch Admin can only view and sell available add-ons at assigned locations.

List columns:
- Add-On
- Description
- Price
- Required/Optional
- Minimum and Maximum Quantity
- Category/Subcategory/Product Assignments
- Active Locations
- Status
- Actions

Add/edit fields:
- Unique code
- Name
- Description
- Price
- Required or Optional
- Minimum quantity
- Maximum quantity
- Display order
- Available ON/OFF
- Parent-category assignments
- Subcategory assignments
- Product assignments
- Location availability
- Optional location price override

Rules:
- Require at least one category, subcategory, or product assignment.
- Required add-ons have a minimum quantity of at least 1.
- Maximum quantity cannot be below minimum quantity; price cannot be negative.
- Customer and POS product forms show applicable add-ons after product options.
- Changing an add-on requests a fresh server quote and updates its itemized unit price, quantity, and total.
- Disable unavailable add-ons with a reason and remove stale selections after re-quote.
- Save add-on name, description, unit price, quantity, required status, and total as immutable order-time snapshots.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.3D PRICING & WEIGHT CONFIGURATION
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Provide one Main Admin section for entering every ingredient and weight price used by dynamic quotes.

Tabs:
- Flavour Pricing
- Egg/Eggless Pricing
- Flour Type Pricing
- Sugar Type Pricing
- Weight Pricing
- Price Preview

Common pricing-table columns:
- Cake or Apply-to-All Cakes
- Category: Cakes / GUNUCO PREMIUM / Custom Cakes
- Option Name
- 500g Price
- 1kg Price
- 2kg Price
- 3kg Price
- Available ON/OFF
- Effective From
- Updated By
- Updated At

Default controls:
- Default option radio button for each ingredient group
- Default Weight, initially 500g
- Default Quantity, initially 1
- Starting Price preview
- Lowest-default validation result

Initial defaults for catalogue cakes:
- Sugar Type: Mishri
- Egg Preference: Egg
- Flour Type: Maida
- Weight: 500g
- Quantity: 1

Main Admin can later change a cake's default selections. Before saving, the system verifies every default is active for that cake and weight and that the default combination is the lowest available starting-price combination.

Weight Pricing tab:

```text
| Weight | Cakes | GUNUCO PREMIUM | Custom Cakes | Price Contribution | Available |
| 500 g  | Yes   | Yes             | Optional     | [amount]           | [ON/OFF]  |
| 1 kg   | Yes   | Yes             | Yes          | [amount]           | [ON/OFF]  |
| 2 kg   | Yes   | Yes             | Yes          | [amount]           | [ON/OFF]  |
| 3 kg   | Yes   | Yes             | Yes          | [amount]           | [ON/OFF]  |
| 4-10kg | No    | No              | Yes          | [amount]           | [ON/OFF]  |
| >10 kg | No    | No              | Request Only | Manual Quote       | [ON/OFF]  |
```

Weight rules:
- Cakes and GUNUCO PREMIUM use fixed weights: 500g, 1kg, 2kg, and 3kg maximum.
- Custom Cakes use configured weights from 500g through 10kg.
- Main Admin may enable or disable each weight and set its price contribution.
- For a Custom Cake above 10kg, customer selects `Above 10kg`, enters the required weight, and submits a quote request.
- Above-10kg requests cannot receive an automatic final price or automatic acceptance.
- Main Admin reviews production feasibility, delivery handling, lead time, and price, then sends a manual quote.
- Customer must approve the quote before payment and production.
- Quantity means the number of cakes; weight means the weight of each cake. Keep these as separate fields.

Catalogue ingredient pricing example:

```text
| Ingredient Group | Option      | 500g | 1kg | 2kg | 3kg |
| Sugar Type       | Mishri      | +40  | +80 | +160| +240|
| Sugar Type       | Stevia      | +60  | +120| +240| +360|
| Flour Type       | Maida       | +100 | +200| +400| +600|
| Flour Type       | Wheat Flour | +150 | +300| +600| +900|
| Egg Preference   | Egg         | +100 | +200| +400| +600|
| Egg Preference   | Eggless     | +150 | +300| +600| +900|
```

Custom Cake 1kg pricing basis:
- Main Admin enters the base and all ingredient prices for 1kg only.
- For 500g through 10kg, default ingredient price is `1kg Ingredient Price x Requested Weight in kg`.
- Example: a 1kg Wheat Flour contribution of Rs 300 becomes Rs 1,500 for a 5kg Custom Cake.
- Main Admin can override the calculated quote for design complexity, structure, decoration, or special handling and must enter an override reason.
- Above 10kg always remains a manual quote.
- The customer sees both the calculated 1kg-based amount and any approved manual adjustment.
- For unpaid requests use Approve Quote, Request Clarification, or Reject. Approve Quote never marks the order Accepted; only customer quote approval plus successful Full or Advance payment accepts it for production.

Price Preview:
- Main Admin selects a cake, flavour, Egg/Eggless, flour type, sugar type, weight, and quantity.
- Show the same itemized dynamic price breakdown that the customer will see.
- Prevent publishing a cake if no active price exists for a required option or allowed weight.
- For catalogue cakes, preview uses the exact selected-weight price column.
- For Custom Cakes, preview shows the 1kg basis, weight multiplier, and manual adjustment separately.

Quota rules:
- Stop accepting the cake when its daily quantity quota is reached.
- Show an alert at 80 percent utilization.
- Reset usage at midnight in the production house timezone.

GUNUCO PREMIUM rules:
- Owner Admin and Main Admin can add a cake to or remove a cake from GUNUCO PREMIUM; Branch Admin cannot.
- Premium cakes use the same flavour, Egg/Eggless, sugar type, flour type, size, quantity, automatic pricing, same-day, availability, and quota controls as Cakes.
- Display a visible GUNUCO PREMIUM badge in the customer catalogue, admin tables, production queue, and orders.
- Premium availability and daily limits are controlled independently from Cakes and Custom Cakes.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.4 CUSTOM CAKES
------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Review, price, accept, and produce customer-configured cakes.

Request fields:
- Customer Name
- Mobile Number
- Email
- Fulfilment Method: Pickup-at-Store or Doorstep-Delivery
- Delivery Address (required only for Doorstep-Delivery)
- Flavour (required)
- Egg Preference: Egg or Eggless (required)
- Sugar Type (required)
- Flour Type: Maida or Wheat Flour (required)
- Size/Weight (required)
- Requested Custom Weight in kg (shown only for Above 10kg)
- Quantity stepper (required, minimum 1)
- Occasion or Theme
- Reference Image
- Cake Message
- Special Instructions
- Requested Delivery Date and Time
- Quoted Price
- Payment Method (selected when a payable final quote is available)
- Payment Status (pre-payment requests remain Pending)

Admin actions:
- Accept
- Request Clarification
- Reject with Reason
- Confirm Price
- Move to Production
- Assign Delivery Partner when ready

Validation rules:
- Block submission when flavour, egg preference, sugar type, flour type, size, or quantity is missing.
- Allow requested delivery from exactly 3 days through exactly 30 days after order time.
- Disable dates before the minimum and after the maximum in the date picker.
- Revalidate the 72-to-720-hour window on the server before creating the request.
- Standard Custom Cake weights up to 10kg can use automatic ingredient pricing.
- Above-10kg requests require Main Admin feasibility review and manual quote approval before acceptance.
- Enforce the daily Custom Cakes quota.
- Show the customer a clear reason when a request cannot be submitted.

Custom cake statuses:
- Not Accepted
- Clarification Requested
- Rejected
- Accepted
- Preparing
- Packed
- Ready for Delivery
- Assigned
- Picked Up
- Out for Delivery
- Delivered
- Cancelled

